Hello!

I was curious what y'alls advice might be regarding handling items with different numbers of response categories due to low endorsement rates for some categories on some items.

I am running DIF on a scale that was originally 5 response categories for all items, but due to low endorsement I have had to collapse some of the items down to 3 or 4 categories.

I know in flexMIRT you can run DIF with different categories, you just need to specify how many categories each item has. Is there a way to do this with the MIRT package? If not, what is best practice for dealing with this issue? Currently I am just collapsing all items down to 3 categories, but I wasn't sure if there was a better approach.

Thanks!
Savanna

